# Requirements: tidydown

**Defined:** 2026-02-07
**Core Value:** Users should never have to manually organize their Downloads folder again.

## v1 Requirements

Requirements for manual sort command feature. Each maps to roadmap phases.

### CLI Commands

- [ ] **CLI-01**: User can run `tidydown sort` command to trigger manual re-organization
- [ ] **CLI-02**: User can run `tidydown sort --dry-run` to preview changes without moving files
- [ ] **CLI-03**: User can run `tidydown sort --execute` to apply changes after preview
- [ ] **CLI-04**: User can run `tidydown sort --undo` to reverse the last sort operation

### Dry-Run Mode

- [ ] **DRY-01**: Sort command defaults to dry-run mode showing preview of changes
- [ ] **DRY-02**: Dry-run output shows each file that would be moved with destination category
- [ ] **DRY-03**: Dry-run output shows summary count (X files would be moved)
- [ ] **DRY-04**: `--execute` flag is required to actually move files

### Progress Display

- [ ] **PRG-01**: Sort command shows TUI progress bar during operation
- [ ] **PRG-02**: Progress displays current file and percentage complete
- [ ] **PRG-03**: Progress shows real-time counter (Processed X/Y files)
- [ ] **PRG-04**: TUI falls back to simple text output in non-TTY environments

### File Processing

- [x] **PROC-01**: Sort command only processes files in watch folder root (not subdirectories)
- [x] **PROC-02**: Sort command skips files already in category folders
- [x] **PROC-03**: Sort command respects exclude patterns from config
- [ ] **PROC-04**: Sort command respects existing conflict resolution strategy from config
- [x] **PROC-05**: Sort command handles symbolic links safely (skips by default)

### Coordination

- [ ] **COORD-01**: Sort command acquires lock file before processing to prevent watcher interference
- [ ] **COORD-02**: Background watcher checks for lock file and skips processing when sort is active
- [ ] **COORD-03**: Lock file is released after sort completes (even on error)
- [ ] **COORD-04**: Stale lock files (>1 hour old) are automatically cleaned up

### Verbose Logging

- [ ] **LOG-01**: Sort command shows each file move with color-coded category
- [ ] **LOG-02**: Verbose output shows source and destination paths
- [ ] **LOG-03**: Summary shows total files moved, skipped, and errors
- [ ] **LOG-04**: Errors are logged with context but don't abort entire operation

### Undo / Rollback

- [ ] **UNDO-01**: Sort operation logs all moves to `~/.local/share/tidydown/history.json`
- [ ] **UNDO-02**: History log includes timestamp, source path, and destination path for each move
- [ ] **UNDO-03**: `tidydown sort --undo` reverses moves from the last sort operation
- [ ] **UNDO-04**: Undo operation handles cases where files no longer exist at destination

### User Confirmation

- [ ] **CONF-01**: Sort command prompts for confirmation before executing moves
- [ ] **CONF-02**: Confirmation shows count of files that will be moved
- [ ] **CONF-03**: `--yes` flag skips confirmation for scripting scenarios

### Exit Codes

- [ ] **EXIT-01**: Sort command returns 0 on success (even if no files moved)
- [ ] **EXIT-02**: Sort command returns non-zero on critical errors
- [ ] **EXIT-03**: Individual file move errors don't cause non-zero exit (graceful degradation)

## v2 Requirements

Deferred to future release. Tracked but not in current roadmap.

### [Enhancement-01]

Age filtering - `--older-than 30d` flag to only process files older than N days

### [Enhancement-02]

Size filtering - `--min-size 1MB` to skip tiny files

### [Enhancement-03]

Operation history - `tidydown sort --history` to show past sort operations

### [Enhancement-04]

Recursive mode - `--recursive` flag to organize files in subdirectories

## Out of Scope

Explicitly excluded. Documented to prevent scope creep.

| Feature | Reason |
|---------|--------|
| Windows support | Platform-specific service integration (launchd/systemd only) |
| Automatic categorization of unknown types | Files without matching extensions stay in root |
| Network filesystem support | Local filesystems only |
| Auto-delete files | HIGH data loss risk, users should delete manually |
| Real-time monitoring during sort | TUI progress bar sufficient, adds complexity |
| Interactive selective sorting | HIGH complexity, defer to v2+ |
| Date-based organization | Alternative to categories, defer to v2+ |
| Smart duplicate detection | Hash-based dedup, may be overkill |

